DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((9/(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((x^2-2*x+2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 11) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 11)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -1, 1, 9})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(-infinity, 13] U ((-infinity, 13] U {-8, -1, 1, 9} U (-infinity, 11)) U (-infinity, 13] U ((-infinity, 13] U (-infinity, 11))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(-infinity, 11) U ((-infinity, 13])");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(1, 5) U ({-10, -9, -7, -2, 0} U ({-10, -9, -7, -2, 0})) U {-10, -9, -7, -2, 0}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(1, 5) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -9, -7, -2, 0}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -9, -7, -2, 0})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-10, -9, -7, -2, 0} - (((1, 5) U {-10, -9, -7, -2, 0})))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`16/8+19*19`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('363'),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`16+7-14-2`]? [_____]{Real(7.)}
---

[`4+15-15-7`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>-3,width=>8}
---

[`18+2+5*8`] is equal to [_____]{Real(60.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 1 < x < 5\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -9, -7, -2, 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup (B \cup (B)) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B - ((A \cup B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 11\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 13\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, -1, 1, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap A \cap C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup (B \cup C \cup A) \cup B \cup (B \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`A \cup (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 4, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -5, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -5, 1, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 1, -4>") x Compute("<3, 4, -5>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 4, -5>") . Compute("<-5, 1, -4>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 4, -5>") x Compute("<-5, 1, -4>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, 4, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, 9, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -9, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, 9, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-8, -9, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, 9, -1>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 9, -1>") . Compute("<-8, -9, -2>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
